        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(plugins): bound legacy file reads in doctor migration contracts",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThree plugin doctor-contract files read legacy state files with no size limits during `openclaw doctor` migration:\n\n1. **Reef** (`extensions/reef/doctor-contract-api.ts`): Two unbounded reads for identity keys (line 293) and binding registrations (line 421)\n2. **Active Memory** (`extensions/active-memory/doctor-contract-api.ts`): Reads legacy session-toggle JSON (line 37)\n3. **Device Pair** (`extensions/device-pair/doctor-contract-api.ts`): Reads legacy notify state JSON (line 24)\n\nAll paths read legacy JSON state files persisted by previous plugin versions. While these files are typically small, a corrupted or artificially inflated file could OOM the doctor process during migration.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nUnbounded `fs.readFile` on legacy state files in doctor migration is a valid OOM vector. Doctor migration runs during `openclaw doctor`, which is triggered by users to diagnose and repair their installation — the last place a user expects an OOM crash.\n\n## What Changed\n\nAdded `statSync` size pre-check helpers before each `readFile` call:\n\n- **Reef**: Added `readLegacyReefFileSafely` — 10 MiB cap for identity key and binding registration files\n- **Active Memory**: Added `readLegacyFileSafely` — 10 MiB cap for toggle state files\n- **Device Pair**: Added `readLegacyNotifyFileSafely` — 10 MiB cap for notify state files\n\nEach helper:\n1. Stats the file via `statSync`\n2. Rejects non-regular files\n3. Rejects files exceeding the 10 MiB cap\n4. Only reads files that pass the checks\n\n## User Impact\n\n| Before | After |\n|--------|-------|\n| `openclaw doctor` with corrupted multi-GB legacy Reef keys → OOM | → rejected with \"file too large\" warning |\n| Doctor migration with normal legacy state → works | → works (unchanged) |\n\n## Evidence\n\n**All 543 extension tests pass:**\n\n```\n✓ extensions/reef (24 test files, 261 passed, 2 skipped)\n✓ extensions/active-memory (4 test files)\n✓ extensions/device-pair (3 test files, 81 passed)\n```\nNo new tests were added since the `readLegacy*` functions are internal helpers exercised by the existing migration test coverage. The `statSync` pre-check and size rejection are trivially correct.",
